  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nAttributes applied through an alias are now found on older compilers (#82, closes #81). The generator build used by Roslyn 4.0–4.3 hosts (for example the .NET 6 SDK and Visual Studio 2022 up to 17.3) only recognised \\[GenerateImposter] by the name as written. When every attribute in a project went through an alias (using Generate = Imposter.Abstractions.GenerateImposterAttribute;, or a global using alias), no imposter was generated. Newer compilers were not affected.\n\nPerformance\n\nFaster attribute discovery on Roslyn 4.0–4.3 hosts (#82). Discovery no longer re-reads every assembly attribute for each \\[GenerateImposter], so its cost grows linearly instead of with the square of the attribute count. With 800 attributes, it drops from about 480 ms and 138 MB per run to about 3 ms and 2 MB.",
